1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,818
The evidence meeting was held in a cottage upstairs from the field station, in a room with a rug, a cupboard, and a bathroom nobody had cleaned.

2
00:00:08,818 --> 00:00:15,812
“This is a story about moisture, not about politics,” the hydrologist said.

3
00:00:15,812 --> 00:00:20,426
“Nothing on this table was measured in a theater.”

4
00:00:20,426 --> 00:00:32,674
The belief in the old model had a theatrical quality: an angel of a forecast, a handful of statistics, and an insect of a detail that everyone ignored.

5
00:00:32,674 --> 00:00:40,887
An airplane passed overhead; downstairs, a dolphin on a poster watched the room.

6
00:00:40,887 --> 00:00:47,092
The exterior of the argument was oily and wavy, like a waterproof sheet.

7
00:00:47,092 --> 00:00:56,860
A monkey in a cage, a goat on a rope, and a pistol in a drawer were, in the report, mere illustrations.

8
00:00:56,860 --> 00:01:05,184
“Put the two together,” Maya said, “and you have the emptiness of a takeoff without a runway.”

9
00:01:05,184 --> 00:01:13,332
The sailing club had kept a boiler and a dryer in the same cupboard as their records, and the records had survived.

10
00:01:13,332 --> 00:01:18,442
“Watertight, not waterproof,” the boatman said.

11
00:01:18,442 --> 00:01:28,925
“That is the difference between a claim and a fact.” A crush of photographs lay on the table, each one wavy with damp.

12
00:01:28,925 --> 00:01:38,453
The fragmentary evidence was enough for one conclusion: the district needed a skyscraper of data reduced to a mouthful of truth.

13
00:01:38,453 --> 00:01:49,886
Two of the five gauges were off by almost four per cent, and a centigrade reading from the north bank had been taken while the water was still rising.

14
00:01:49,886 --> 00:01:54,336
“We do not need nudity of detail,” Lin said.

15
00:01:54,336 --> 00:02:07,213
“We need a hairy, awkward, exact account of what happened on the night of the flood.” The meeting ended with a single page, and the page included the river's own answer.

16
00:02:07,213 --> 00:02:21,181
Nothing on the table was mere decoration: a handful of statistics from the upstairs room, a belief written on the exterior of the cottage, and an oily wavy record from the sailing club.

17
00:02:21,181 --> 00:02:35,388
An airplane, a dolphin, a monkey, an insect: the city's icons had nothing to do with moisture, and the emptiness of the report was the emptiness of a takeoff without a runway.

18
00:02:35,388 --> 00:02:39,968
The dryer, the boiler, and the rug were all on the list.

19
00:02:39,968 --> 00:02:50,286
Almost every sentence in the file had one statistic behind it: an eyebrow raised, a woollen rug, and a record kept ashore.

20
00:02:50,286 --> 00:03:01,974
Four of the five items on the shelf were probably included by mistake, and the start of the action was to put them off the table while the need for moisture data stayed on it.

21
00:03:01,974 --> 00:03:07,598
There was no talk of a view from the tower, or of the water as scenery.

22
00:03:07,598 --> 00:03:17,872
The radio gave a pop and went quiet; downstream, past the toilet, an apartment block stood empty.
